WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:36.280
[Music]

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:42.760
[Narrator:] This is human rabies introduced by the 
bite of a rabid dog.

00:00:42.766 --> 00:00:47.540
[Music]

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:51.760
These are actual cases, all of the patients were dead within 12 hours

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.160
after these pictures were taken.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:01:00.700
Rabies is a virus disease that affects the central nervous system, where it destroys the vital centers.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.900
This youngster could not understand what was wrong with her;

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:12.620
did not realize that death was inevitable.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:19.100
In dogs, the symptoms are variable but usually in 
the early stages, sudden movement or noise

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.020
[Two loud hand claps]

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:26.700
cause exaggerated nervous responses.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:39.280
As the disease progresses, paralysis of the jaw 
and throat may occur.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:46.240
At this stage, the dog is unable to swallow, and saliva drools from his mouth.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:54.380
Some hours later, the paralysis becomes more general, causing loss of muscular control.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:59.100
Finally, death occurs due to paralysis of the vital centers.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:12.160
This dog does not drool at all; however, the symptoms of rabies are beginning to show,

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.540
The virus is in the saliva and the animal is infectious.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:21.460
The dog may show a marked change of personality and may swallow bits of wood, stones, or feathers.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:27.040
Frequently he will bite animate or inanimate 
objects.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.560
In furious rabies, the dog may run about aimlessly attacking other animals and humans,

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.520
frequently causing severe outbreaks of the disease.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:41.420
However, the form shown in this film, called dumb rabies, may be equally dangerous

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:45.460
because the characteristic symptoms are not evident.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:59.620
Rabies may be transmitted by infected foxes,

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:03.020
domestic cats,

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:09.600
dogs, and other biting animals, although all warm- blooded animals are susceptible to the disease.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:16.000
Because of the close association between dogs 
and humans, the dog is our chief concern

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.620
in considering the rabies problem.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:28.620
This is any American community, lots of youngsters and lots of dogs.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:35.740
Certainly no one is thinking about rabies, but rabies is here, carried by this forlorn stray dog

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:41.680
from who knows where.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:47.560
Already he has bitten the pet dog. This is the beginning of an outbreak of rabies,

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:53.960
nothing spectacular, nothing sensational, no snarling, frenzied animal.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:01.540
But the rabies virus has been introduced into the 
everyday life of this community.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:08.660
A few weeks later it begins to show itself. The boy's friendly, playful pet turns mean,

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:18.100
bites his master, and several neighborhood children.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:24.780
Within a few weeks, the pet dog dies; autopsy and subsequent laboratory examinations

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:34.700
prove beyond a doubt that the cause of death was rabies.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:41.520
There is no choice now but to give each of the bitten children a long series of anti-rabies injections.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:47.580
Most of them will be protected, but some may not.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:59.400
This could have been prevented through a sound 
rabies control program.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.400
What is wrong with this community?

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:09.833
[Woman 1:] I take good care my dog; he hardly 
ever goes out of doors. Why, he can't get rabies.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:16.500
[Man 1:] Rabies? Listen I've raised dogs all my life, 
I never heard of a case of rabies.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:22.100
[Woman 2:] Well, I don't think rabies will ever be 
much a problem here.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:26.580
[Narrator:] That was the trouble with the 
community--apathy and ignorance.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:30.800
But after they did have an outbreak of rabies, the 
whole story changed.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:36.440
Now the people ask that something be done.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:40.133
To the local board of health came groups of citizens to discuss a program

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:45.700
to eliminate rabies from their community.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.900
The board appointed a public health veterinarian 
to direct the program.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:03.800
His first move was to get pet owners to have their 
animals vaccinated.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:08.400
[Government vehicle with public address system:] [?] Memorial Park, let's get rid of rabies.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:12.066
Bring your dog to the community-sponsored vaccination clinic

00:06:12.066 --> 00:06:15.066
today at the Robert Banks Memorial Park.

00:06:15.066 --> 00:06:20.732
Everybody, bring your pets today, let's get rid of 
rabies.

00:06:20.733 --> 00:06:27.666
[Narrator:] The response was gratifying. Pedigreed dogs and mongrels, high-bred and low-bred,

00:06:27.666 --> 00:06:35.480
but each one loved by someone who wanted his dog safe from rabies.

00:06:37.566 --> 00:06:43.400
Modern rabies vaccines cause little discomfort to the dog but are highly effective,

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:49.800
giving a much longer period of immunity than the older types.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:54.666
In preference to the community-sponsored vaccination clinic, many people preferred

00:06:54.666 --> 00:06:57.899
to have their private veterinarians vaccinate their pets.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:03.233
As the immunization proceeded, another phase of the program was in action,

00:07:03.233 --> 00:07:08.999
the picking up of stray dogs, a real threat to the community.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.333
Well-trained dog wardens were given the responsibility of picking up strays

00:07:12.333 --> 00:07:16.399
and taking them to the local animal shelter.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:20.666
This was a well-constructed, up-to-date building where humane treatment was emphasized

00:07:20.666 --> 00:07:25.380
and the dogs kept in clean quarters.

00:07:33.966 --> 00:07:41.120
Dogs suspected of having rabies were isolated and kept under observation.

00:07:41.133 --> 00:07:47.133
The removal of strays and the vaccination of pets soon showed definite progress,

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:49.733
but there was still one more factor to consider.

00:07:49.733 --> 00:07:58.533
The woods at the edge of town offered harborage for foxes, which had been very abundant that year.

00:07:58.533 --> 00:08:03.633
Cooperating with the rabies control program, the state wildlife commission agreed

00:08:03.633 --> 00:08:06.633
to reduce the number of foxes in this area.

00:08:06.633 --> 00:08:10.466
Excessive numbers of foxes in a given area form an ideal situation

00:08:10.466 --> 00:08:14.080
for an explosive outbreak of rabies.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:26.640
Scientific reduction of their numbers is good 
conservation practice and good rabies control.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:40.600
So as time went on, this community gained increasing control over its rabies problem.

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:47.933
The citizens learned the truth of the statement that public health begins with the people themselves.

00:08:47.933 --> 00:08:50.699
[Woman 1:] Yes, we learned the hard way.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:53.766
But now we've protected our pets from rabies.

00:08:53.766 --> 00:08:56.766
[Man 1:] Well, I sure was wrong.

00:08:56.766 --> 00:09:01.266
Having a dog vaccinated against rabies is a man's obligation to his neighbors.

00:09:01.266 --> 00:09:06.532
[Woman 2:] Well, I guess we've all learned, rabies 
can become a problem in any community.

00:09:06.533 --> 00:09:11.333
[Man 2:] Now we're rid of rabies and it'll never get 
back.

00:09:11.333 --> 00:09:16.266
[Narrator:] Well, that's a pretty strong statement, 
rabies can always be re-introduced.

00:09:16.266 --> 00:09:22.100
For instance, a new family moves to town from a 
community where rabies is present.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:33.433
The pet dog has been exposed, but symptoms have not begun to show.

00:09:33.433 --> 00:09:39.766
Then a few weeks later he becomes irritable and 
begins to wander aimlessly.

00:09:39.766 --> 00:09:47.332
[Sounds of barking]

00:09:47.333 --> 00:09:52.266
This time the people know what to do.

00:09:52.266 --> 00:10:03.866
[Music]

00:10:03.866 --> 00:10:07.866
As later tests proved, the new dog was indeed rabid.

00:10:07.866 --> 00:10:12.599
In the course of his wanderings, he had bitten two 
pet dogs.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:16.266
One of these had been vaccinated only three months before.

00:10:16.266 --> 00:10:20.599
He was re-vaccinated and confined to his yard for 30 days.

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:25.866
If no symptoms showed in that time, he would be 
safe.

00:10:25.866 --> 00:10:30.866
The other bitten dog had not been vaccinated, so he would be held six months for observation.

00:10:30.866 --> 00:10:33.999
Thus a second outbreak was avoided.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:41.333
And this same three-part control procedure-- vaccination of all pets, keeping stray animals

00:10:41.333 --> 00:10:46.533
off the streets, and controlling wild animals in the outskirts of the community--

00:10:46.533 --> 00:10:52.433
this same pattern of rabies control will succeed for any community or county or even state,

00:10:52.433 --> 00:10:59.266
providing it has the whole-hearted backing of a public with a real desire to stamp out rabies.

00:10:59.266 --> 00:11:06.400
[Music]

